# Speed and correctness (owner 2026-10-29; cards 3.44 / 3.45 / Phase 4)

Full text: `docs/plans/parallel-sessions-guide.md` §7–§10 and `docs/RUN-WITHOUT-CLAUDE.md` §5–§9. Binding for implementer, reviewer, subagents and lead. These override AGENTS.md session protocol step 4 (do **not** run the Phase 0.2 full lifecycle locally). They **never** weaken the Definition of Done, code correctness, or completeness.

Speed means:
1. Write **100% complete, production-grade code and tests** for your part first (zero stubs, zero skipped tests, zero missing rules).
2. Prove **your part** locally in 1–3 minutes (targeted tests + touched workspace typecheck + changed-file lint/prettier + app browser suite for UI).
3. Push **once**, run the independent **Reviewer subagent in parallel while CI is running**, prepare the review and merge docs during the CI run, and merge immediately with a docs-only commit once CI turns green.

## Hard quality guardrails (never compromise for speed)

- **Never** write incomplete code, partial use cases, `TODO`s, stubs, mock data, `any`, or `as unknown as` casts.
- **Never** skip, weaken, or stub a test named in the plan or required by `parallel-sessions-guide.md` §11 / `RUN-WITHOUT-CLAUDE.md` §7 (happy path, validation error, permission denied, cross-org denied, cross-location, concurrency/idempotency, timezone/date edge cases).
- **Never** push before running and seeing green output on every test file you created or modified.
- If a plan test or requirement is ambiguous or needs a product decision: **stop and ask**. Never guess or invent a weaker rule.

## Never (time-wasters that burn 15–40 minutes)

- Root `npm run lint` / `typecheck` / `test` / `build` locally. CI runs the whole monorepo.
- Push to learn if a test or build fails. **CI is not a debugger.**
- Guess-and-push (tiny edit → wait 20 min → tiny edit).
- Sit idle waiting for CI before starting the T1/T2 review — always run the independent Reviewer while CI is running.
- Run independent parallel-lane cards sequentially when separate worktrees are available; push independent branches concurrently so their CI runs overlap.
- Rebase a second time only because `main` moved (`card:check` INFO is fine; the lead merges `origin/main`).
- Use `--no-verify` or `git commit -a` in `banijjik`.

## Before every code push (1–3 minutes; report real command output)

1. Verify every file, contract, validation schema, i18n key (`bn` + `en`), and test listed in the frozen plan/Refresh for this part is 100% complete.
2. Run the test files you changed or added (API: `npm.cmd test -w @banijjik/api -- <file> --maxWorkers=1` with the env vars in `RUN-WITHOUT-CLAUDE.md` §9). If you edited a shared add-only file (contracts permissions, i18n catalogs, `routes/*.ts`), also run the neighbouring contract/catalog test.
3. Run `npx.cmd turbo run typecheck --filter=<touched workspace>` — not the whole repo. If workspace package types changed or you switched branches, run `npx.cmd turbo run build --filter="./packages/*"` first so `dist/` is never stale.
4. Run `npx.cmd eslint --max-warnings 0 <changed files>` and `npx.cmd prettier --check <changed files>`.
5. **Screen or `*.browser.test.ts` change:** build `@banijjik/api` first (`npx.cmd turbo run build --filter=@banijjik/api`), then run that app's browser suite locally (`VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 npm.cmd run test:browser -w @banijjik/<app>`).

## While CI is running (zero-idle pipeline for Lead & Subagents)

1. When using subagents in Antigravity, always pass `Model: "flash"` (Gemini Flash) and keep roles strictly separated (an Implementer subagent never reviews its own code).
2. The moment the code commit is pushed (`git push -u origin s/<card>-<part>-<slug>`) and CI starts on GitHub:
   - Immediately launch the independent **Reviewer** subagent on `git diff "origin/main...s/<card>-<part>-<slug>"` against the plan, `AGENTS.md`, and §11 / §7 checklists.
   - Write `docs/handoffs/<card>-review-R1.md` and prepare the `docs/handoffs/<card>.md`, `docs/STATUS.md`, and `docs/LEAD-STATE.md` updates while CI is in progress.
3. As soon as CI finishes green (and if review Verdict is `PASS`), commit the `docs/` files (`paths-ignore: ["docs/**"]` skips a second CI run) and fast-forward `main` immediately.

## After a red CI job (read the failed **test name** or step, not just the job colour)

| What failed | Do | Do not |
|---|---|---|
| Known flake (`ordered-event-worker.test.ts`, `sync-indexes.test.ts`, `main.test.ts`, admin `auth-flow`) OR GitHub 20m runner timeout during `Build` after `Lint`, `Typecheck` and `Test` all passed | `gh run rerun <runId> --failed` **once** | New commit |
| A file you touched | Reproduce that file locally, fix completely, verify locally, **one** push | Guess-and-push |
| A file you did not touch, not a known flake | Stop; write it in the STATUS handoff | Touch it |

A second failure of the same test is a real bug: reproduce locally, then one push. Never keep rerunning CI in a loop.

## Windows / PowerShell hygiene (avoid wasted command retries)

- Use `npm.cmd`, `npx.cmd`, and `& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe"` in PowerShell so `.ps1` execution policy never blocks a command.
- Always quote git revision ranges containing `..` (e.g. `"origin/main..HEAD"`, `"origin/main...HEAD"`) so PowerShell does not parse `..` as an integer range operator.
- In Storefront/Node tests on Windows that send custom `Host` headers (`*.localhost`) over loopback, use `node:http` to `127.0.0.1` (`fetchStorefront` helper) because Node global `fetch` (undici) overrides custom `Host` headers.

## Docs-only

A commit that changes only `docs/` starts no CI (`paths-ignore: ["docs/**"]`). Do not wait for CI after a docs-only push; `card:check` uses the last **code** commit's green run.

```text
❌ BAD: push untested/incomplete code → wait 20 min → fail → tiny edit → wait 20 min
❌ BAD: skip tests / stub logic / weaken assertions so CI stays green
❌ BAD: wait 20 min doing nothing while CI runs, then start T1 review after CI finishes
✅ GOOD: 100% complete code + tests → 2 min targeted local check → 1 push → T1 review + docs prep IN PARALLEL with CI → instant merge when green
```
